WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
G-M, H, I-T. I-T! T-D-I-A-R-Q-F-R-N. [Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday. It's Tuesday, the day I answer real questions from real nerdfighters.]

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.540
Let's get right to it. Will you do sharpie face?

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.485
-Yeah, I guess, but only for the answers.

00:00:07.485 --> 00:00:10.520
-How involved do you plan to be in the making of the TFiOS movie?

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.730
-I'll be involved in any way that I can be helpful, but I know that I'm not, like, a movie person.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.640
-Wait, they're making a movie out of The Fault in Our Stars?

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.800
-Yes, the nice people at FOX 2000 auctioned the movie rights to the Fault in Our Stars,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.539
So hopefully they will make it. It's too soon to get excited, but keep your fingers crossed! My face is burning.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:26.220
-Will you ever come to the Netherlands again?

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.640
-Yes. In fact, I'm going to the Netherlands this week. There will be a nerdfighter gathering in

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.840
Amsterdam on Friday night. More info in the doobly-doo.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.469
-Have you ever been drunk? I don't know, I mean, not like really drunk.

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:36.520
-Have you ever been to Mardi gras in New Orleans?

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.219
-All right, yeah, I have been really drunk.

00:00:38.219 --> 00:00:40.860
-Why don't you ever do champagne poppers anymore?

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.119
-I just started to feel like I'm a grown man

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.700
Trying to make video blogs that can be taken seriously

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.560
And champagne poppers just aren't part of that brand— What, the nerdfighter Kiva group hit

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.860
$500,000? Shibam! Ow.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.380
Ow, that was uncomfortable.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.140
-Have you had any experience with drugs?

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:59.300
-Yeah, I've had quite a lot of experience, actually. For instance, on several occasions this class of drugs called

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.480
Antibiotics did an amazing job of helping me to not be dead.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.940
-Do you get annoyed when people correct your grammar?

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:06.630
-Oh, you mean like how I just split an infinitive?

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:11.060
I only get annoyed when people use grammar as a way of humiliating other people in

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.619
Youtube comments rather than using grammar for what it's

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:18.659
supposed to be used for, which is to make language as clear and intelligible as possible.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.140
-What's the moment when you realized you were old?

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:25.580
-Let me ask you a question: If I'm so old, how come my face is covered in Sharpie?

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:28.290
-Who do you think should play Hazel and Augustus in a movie of The Fault in Our Stars?

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:33.080
-I have no idea because of course I know nothing of contemporary actors and actresses, like in my mind's

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:38.120
imagination, Drew Barrymore is still 17 years old. More importantly who would you want to play

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.680
Hazel and Augustus in the movie?

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.440
-Is The Fault In Our Stars still on the bestseller list?

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:46.889
-Yes, it's currently number 2 on the New York Times bestseller list behind only Hugo Cabret. Damn you, Hugo. Just kidding.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:50.200
I really liked that book. By the way, this smells really...toxic.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.160
Plus it makes my crazy eyes look crazier.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.500
-2,300 librarians just went on strike in Toronto. What say you?

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:00.500
-I stand with the librarians! Unless they don't want a guy with sharpie face standing with them, in which case

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:02.700
I will quietly support them from a distance.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.020
-Favorite part about writing a book?

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:04.780
-Having written.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:05.660
-Was Hamlet mad?

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.160
-No.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.740
-Any fishing boat proceeds this year?

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.920
-Alas, I am again fishing boat proceeds-less.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:10.460
Babies?

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.020
-Babies!

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.440
-Are you working on a new book yet?

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:15.340
-No, I got to finish my stupid bad zombie story first.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.860
-All-time favorite Greek Philosopher.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.320
-Maybe obvious if you've read The Fault in Out Stars but Zeno.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.780
-What do Batman and sixteen sodiums have in common?

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.180
-Na na na na na na na na na na [John is missing 6 Na's]

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:24.780
-What are your skills in drawing?

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.380
-As you can see, my skills in drawing are legendary.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.020
-Can you recommend any Swedish hip-hop?

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:33.620
-Yes, Afasi och Filthy are great, although best enjoyed if you don't speak Swedish, also Snook.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.620
-Who the eff is Hank?

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.140
-Hank is a cat running for the United States Senate from the great state of Virginia.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.860
-Hey, when are we gonna see your punishment?

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.800
-Hank, while we were on tour you told me that my punishment will strike at the moment

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:46.470
I least expect it. I've been living in fear ever since, but it still hasn't happened,

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.920
so maybe he's forgotten?

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.500
-Why is Hazel called Hazel?

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:52.859
-Because it's an in-between color, and she has an in-between life. In between health and sickness,

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.360
in between adolescence and adulthood, in between swimming and drowning, et cetera.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.680
-What do you think the difference is between a geek and a nerd?

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.990
-Frankly, I think the fact that both self-identifying geeks and nerds are so fascinated with this question

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.760
indicates that we might have quite a lot in common with each other.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:08.900
-Did you ever want to be a teacher?

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:09.660
-Yeah, and now thanks

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:14.790
to Crash Course I kind of can be, and not to geek out or anything, but I am totally living my teacher dream!

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.320
I geeked out, didn't I?

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:20.249
Or did I nerd out? Hank my head is starting to hurt from Sharpie inhalation,

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:22.770
so I'm gonna let the Crash Course theme play us out. Nerdfighters,

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.340
if you haven't checked out the show, please do.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:28.840
Hank, DFTBA. Thanks for helping me get out of the friendzone as if I was ever friend-zoned.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.260
H, I-S-Y-F [Hank, I'll see you Friday.]

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:36.480
[Crash Course theme plays]

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.480
[Crash Course theme fades]

